    cie_r_servicio: "Service",
    cie_nota_paquete: "When the role and the unit went together and the client's list has the package, the package is charged: a single line instead of the two separately. That's how it goes on the invoice.",
    cie_nota_en_paquete: "Of what was proven, {m} goes inside the package: it isn't charged separately.",
    ay_tar_productos_para: "Says what each product Odoo sells is in Centauro: a role, a unit, a driver + unit package, overtime, expenses or something that isn't Executive Protection, and in which modality: full day, half day, transfer or, what Odoo charges per «Month», monthly. Each country with the products of its Odoo category. With this the prices of the Odoo lists are read.",
    ay_tar_productos_cuando: "Once, before the first price-list reading, and whenever Odoo adds a product. What is confirmed is never suggested again by any reading; what is suggested doesn't set a price until it is confirmed.",
    ay_tar_productos_numero: "Confirmed: those that already say what they are and set a price. Suggested: what Centauro proposes from the name, unconfirmed. Missing: those nobody could tell; they are picked one by one.",
    ay_tar_cliente_para: "What a client is charged: the price of each role, each unit and each package in each modality, and where it comes from —the client's list, its country's general list or the product's «Sales price»—. Each country's general lists also open here, even without a client.",
    ay_tar_cliente_cuando: "To check a price before quoting or invoicing. If something is wrong, it is fixed in Odoo and within the hour it is here.",
    ay_tar_tipo_cambio_para: "How many pesos a dollar is worth and, for Brazil, how many reais: for everything a client that pays in dollars —Amazon in Mexico, Amazon Brazil— is charged in dollars and paid in the country's currency: the quote and the proposal, the net expenses on the invoice, the commission and the prices on its list that come from a list in pesos.",
    ay_tar_tipo_cambio_cuando: "When the dollar moves enough to matter. The one you set applies to what comes next; what is already fixed doesn't move. Without the dollar-to-peso rate a quote in dollars can't be authorized in Mexico; without the dollar-to-real rate, a proposal in dollars for Brazil.",
